msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:398
msgid "A new resource was created in response to a safe request."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:399
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `201 (Created)` status code indicates that the request created a new "
"resource.\n"
"\n"
"However, the request method used (`%(method)s`) is defined as a \"safe\" "
"method; that is, it\n"
"should not have any side effects.\n"
"\n"
"Creating resources as a side effect of a safe method can have unintended "
"consequences; for example,\n"
"search engine spiders and similar automated agents often follow links, "
"and intermediaries sometimes\n"
"re-try safe methods when they fail."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:413
msgid "A new resource was created without its location being sent."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:414
msgid ""
"The `201 (Created)` status code indicates that the request created a new "
"resource.\n"
"\n"
"HTTP specifies that the URL of the new resource is to be indicated in the"
" `Location` header,\n"
"but it isn't present in this response."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:424
msgid "This response is partial, but doesn't have a Content-Range header."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:425
msgid ""
"The `206 (Partial Response)` status code indicates that the response "
"content is only partial.\n"
"\n"
"However, for a response to be partial, it needs to have a `Content-Range`"
" header to indicate\n"
"what part of the full response it carries. This response does not have "
"one."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:435
#, python-format
msgid "A successful response to CONNECT can't have a %(field_name)s header."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:436
msgid ""
"A `2xx` response to a `CONNECT` request switches the connection to a "
"tunnel, so what follows the\n"
"header section is tunnelled data, not message content. A server MUST NOT "
"send `Content-Length` or\n"
"`Transfer-Encoding` in such a response, and clients ignore them.\n"
"\n"
"See [RFC 9110 Section 9.3.6](https://www.rfc-"
"editor.org/rfc/rfc9110.html#section-9.3.6)."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:447
msgid "A partial response was sent when it wasn't requested."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:448
msgid ""
"The `206 (Partial Response)` status code indicates that the response "
"content is only partial.\n"
"\n"
"However, the client needs to ask for it with the `Range` header, and the "
"request did not\n"
"include one."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:458
msgid "Redirects need to have a Location header."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:459
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The %(status)s status code redirects users to another URI. The `Location`"
" header is used to\n"
"convey this URI, but a valid one isn't present in this response."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:467
#, python-format
msgid "The %(status)s status code is deprecated."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:468
msgid ""
"When a status code is deprecated, it should not be used, because its "
"meaning is not well-defined\n"
"enough to ensure interoperability."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:476
#, python-format
msgid "The %(status)s status code is reserved."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:477
msgid ""
"Reserved status codes can only be used by future, standard protocol "
"extensions; they are not for\n"
"private use."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:485
#, python-format
msgid "%(status)s is not a standard HTTP status code."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:486
msgid ""
"Non-standard status codes are not well-defined and interoperable. Instead"
" of defining your own\n"
"status code, you should reuse one of the more generic ones; for example, "
"`400` for a client-side\n"
"problem, or `500` for a server-side problem."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:495
msgid "The server didn't understand the request."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:503
msgid "The server has forbidden this request."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:511
#, python-format
msgid "The resource does not allow the %(method)s method."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:512
msgid ""
"The `405 (Method Not Allowed)` status code indicates that the HTTP method"
" is\n"
"known by the origin server but not supported by the target resource."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:520
#, python-format
msgid "%(method)s is not allowed, but the resource lists it in Allow."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:521
msgid ""
"The `405 (Method Not Allowed)` status code indicates that the HTTP method"
" is\n"
"known by the origin server but not supported by the target resource.\n"
"\n"
"However, the `Allow` header field listed in the response contains the "
"method used,\n"
"indicating that it is allowed."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:532
msgid "The resource could not be found."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:533
msgid "The server couldn't find any resource to serve for the given URI."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:540
msgid "The resource cannot produce a response that is acceptable to the client."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:541
msgid ""
"The `406 (Not Acceptable)` status code indicates that the resource cannot"
" produce a response matching\n"
"the list of acceptable values defined in the request's proactive "
"negotiation header fields, such\n"
"as `Accept`, `Accept-Charset`, `Accept-Encoding`, or `Accept-Language`.\n"
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:551
msgid "The 406 (Not Acceptable) status code appears to be misused."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:552
msgid ""
"The `406 (Not Acceptable)` status code indicates that the request cannot "
"produce a response matching\n"
"the list of acceptable values defined in the request's proactive "
"negotiation header fields.\n"
"\n"
"However, this request didn't contain any proactive negotiation headers "
"(such as `Accept`,\n"
"`Accept-Charset`, `Accept-Encoding`, or `Accept-Language`)."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:563
msgid "The request conflicted with the state of the resource."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:571
msgid "The resource is gone."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:572
msgid ""
"The server previously had a resource at the given URI, but it is no "
"longer there."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:579
msgid "The request content was too large for the server."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:580
msgid ""
"The server rejected the request because the request content sent was too "
"large."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:587
#, python-format
msgid "The server won't accept a URI this long %(uri_len)s."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:588
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The %(status)s status code means that the server can't or won't accept a "
"request-uri this long."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:595
msgid "The resource doesn't support this media type in requests."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:603
msgid "The server returned 418 (I'm a Teapot), an easter egg defined in RFC 2324."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:604
msgid ""
"RFC 2324 was an April Fools' Day RFC that lampooned the various ways HTTP"
" was abused; one such abuse\n"
"was the definition of the application-specific `418 (I'm a Teapot)` "
"status code. In the\n"
"intervening years, this status code has been sometimes implemented as an "
"\"easter egg\".\n"
"\n"
"This status code is not a part of HTTP and hence it might not be "
"supported by some strict\n"
"standards-compliant clients.\n"
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:617
msgid "There was a general server error."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:625
msgid "The server doesn't implement the request method."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:633
msgid "An intermediary encountered an error."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:641
msgid "The server is temporarily unavailable."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:649
msgid "An intermediary timed out."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:657
msgid "The request HTTP version isn't supported."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:665
msgid "The request precondition failed."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:666
msgid ""
"The `412 (Precondition Failed)` status code indicates that one or more "
"conditions given in the\n"
"request header fields (typically, those starting with `If-`)evaluated to "
"false when tested \n"
"on the server."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:675
msgid "The request expectation failed."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:676
msgid ""
"The `417 (Expectation Failed)` status code indicates that the expectation"
" given in the request's\n"
"`Expect` header field could not be met by at least one of the inbound "
"servers."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:684
msgid "The request didn't have any preconditions."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:685
msgid ""
"The `412 (Precondition Failed)` status code indicates that one or more "
"conditions given in the\n"
"request header fields evaluated to false when tested on the server.\n"
"\n"
"However, this request didn't contain any conditional headers (such as "
"`If-Match`, `If-None-Match`,\n"
"`If-Modified-Since`, `If-Unmodified-Since`, or `If-Range`)."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:696
msgid "The request didn't have a Range header."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:697
msgid ""
"The `416 (Range Not Satisfiable)` status code indicates that the set of "
"ranges in the request's\n"
"`Range` header field overlap the current extent of the selected resource."
"\n"
"\n"
"However, this request didn't contain a `Range` header."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:707
msgid "A 416 response to a byte-range request should have a Content-Range header."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:708
msgid ""
"When a server generates a `416 (Range Not Satisfiable)` response to a "
"byte-range request, it\n"
"should send a `Content-Range` header field in the unsatisfied form "
"(`bytes */<length>`), giving the\n"
"current length of the selected representation.\n"
"\n"
"This response didn't include a `Content-Range` header."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:719
msgid "The request didn't have an Expect header."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:720
msgid ""
"The `417 (Expectation Failed)` status code indicates that the expectation"
" given in the request's\n"
"`Expect` header field could not be met by at least one of the inbound "
"servers.\n"
"\n"
"However, this request didn't contain an `Expect` header."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:730
msgid "The server couldn't meet the 100-continue expectation."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:731
msgid ""
"The `417 (Expectation Failed)` status code indicates that the expectation"
" given in the request's\n"
"`Expect` header field could not be met by at least one of the inbound "
"servers.\n"
"\n"
"In this case, the client requested `100-continue`, but the server (or an "
"intermediary) couldn't\n"
"satisfy it."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:742
msgid "The server sent early hints."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:743
msgid ""
"The `103 (Early Hints)` status code allows the server to send some "
"headers before the final response,\n"
"typically to help the client start fetching resources earlier."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:751
msgid "The server supports upload resumption."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:752
msgid ""
"The `104 (Upload Resumption Supported)` status code indicates that the "
"server supports resumable\n"
"uploads."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:760
msgid "The members of a DAV binding have already been enumerated."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:761
msgid ""
"The `208 (Already Reported)` status code can be used inside a DAV: "
"propstat response element to\n"
"avoid enumerating the internal members of multiple bindings to the same "
"collection repeatedly."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:769
msgid ""
"The request was directed at a server that is not able to produce a "
"response."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:770
msgid ""
"The `421 (Misdirected Request)` status code indicates that the request "
"was directed at a server\n"
"that is not able to produce a response. This can happen when a connection"
" is reused."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:778
msgid ""
"The server is unwilling to risk processing a request that might be "
"replayed."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:779
msgid ""
"The `425 (Too Early)` status code indicates that the server is unwilling "
"to risk processing a\n"
"request that might be replayed."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:787
msgid "The origin server requires the request to be conditional."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:788
msgid ""
"The `428 (Precondition Required)` status code indicates that the origin "
"server requires the request\n"
"to be conditional."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:796
msgid "The client has sent too many requests in a given amount of time."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:797
msgid ""
"The `429 (Too Many Requests)` status code indicates that the client has "
"sent too many requests in a\n"
"given amount of time (\"rate limiting\")."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:805
msgid ""
"The server is unwilling to process the request because its headers are "
"too large."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:806
msgid ""
"The `431 (Request Header Fields Too Large)` status code indicates that "
"the server is unwilling to\n"
"process the request because its header fields are too large."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:814
msgid "The resource is unavailable for legal reasons."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:815
msgid ""
"The `451 (Unavailable For Legal Reasons)` status code indicates that the "
"server is denying access to\n"
"the resource as a consequence of a legal demand."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:823
msgid ""
"The server terminated an operation because it encountered an infinite "
"loop."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:824
msgid ""
"The `508 (Loop Detected)` status code indicates that the server "
"terminated an operation because it\n"
"encountered an infinite loop while processing a request with \"Depth: "
"infinity\"."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:832
msgid "The client needs to authenticate to gain network access."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/status.py:833
msgid ""
"The `511 (Network Authentication Required)` status code indicates that "
"the client needs to\n"
"authenticate to gain network access."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/util.py:249
msgid "ahead"
msgstr ""

#: httplint/util.py:251
msgid "behind"
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/__init__.py:276
#, python-format
msgid "\"%(field_name)s\" is not a valid field name."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/__init__.py:277
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Field names are limited to the `token` production in HTTP; i.e., they "
"can't contain parenthesis,\n"
"angle brackets (<>), ampersands (@), commas, semicolons, colons, "
"backslashes (\\), forward\n"
"slashes (/), quotes, square brackets ([]), question marks, equals signs "
"(=), curly brackets ({})\n"
"spaces or tabs."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/__init__.py:288
#, python-format
msgid "The %(field_name)s field value doesn't conform to its specified syntax."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/__init__.py:289
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The value for this field has syntax specified using \n"
"[Augmented BNF](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5234.html),\n"
"but doesn't conform to it. See [the field's ABNF](%(ref_uri)s) for more "
"information.\n"
"\n"
"This error may or may not prevent recipients from parsing the field; "
"fixing it will\n"
"improve interoperability.\n"
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/__init__.py:319
#, python-format
msgid "\"%(field_name)s\" isn't valid in a response."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/__init__.py:320
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `%(field_name)s` field only has meaning in requests. Sending it a "
"response\n"
"doesn't do anything. REDbot (and most recipients) will ignore it."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/__init__.py:328
#, python-format
msgid "\"%(field_name)s\" isn't valid in a request."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/__init__.py:329
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `%(field_name)s` field only has meaning in responses. Sending it in a"
" request\n"
"doesn't do anything. REDbot (and most recipients) will ignore it."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/__init__.py:337
#, python-format
msgid "The %(field_name)s header is deprecated."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/__init__.py:338
#, python-format
msgid ""
"This field is no longer recommended for use, because of interoperability "
"problems and/or\n"
"lack of use. This field should probably be removed.\n"
"\n"
"See [the deprecation notice](%(deprecation_ref)s) for more information."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/codings.py:48
#, python-format
msgid "The '%(coding)s' content-coding is a deprecated alias for '%(standard)s'."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/codings.py:49
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The\n"
"[IANA HTTP Content Coding Registry](https://www.iana.org/assignments"
"/http-parameters/http-parameters.xhtml#content-coding)\n"
"lists `%(coding)s` as deprecated, as an alias for `%(standard)s`.\n"
"\n"
"[RFC 9110](https://www.rfc-"
"editor.org/rfc/rfc9110.html#section-%(section)s) says that a recipient\n"
"SHOULD consider `%(coding)s` to be equivalent to `%(standard)s`, so "
"recipients are likely to\n"
"handle it; however, senders should use `%(standard)s`."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/conneg.py:18
#, python-format
msgid "The q value on '%(item)s' is invalid."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/conneg.py:19
msgid ""
"The `q` parameter must be a decimal number between 0 and 1, with at most "
"3 digits after the\n"
"decimal point (for example, `0.5`). A sign, an exponent, quotes, or a "
"missing leading digit\n"
"aren't allowed."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/cors.py:139
msgid "This is a CORS preflight request."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/cors.py:140
msgid ""
"This is a Cross-Origin Resource Sharing (CORS) preflight request.\n"
"\n"
"A preflight request uses the `OPTIONS` method and includes an `Origin` "
"and `Access-Control-Request-Method`\n"
"header."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/cors.py:150
#, python-format
msgid "The %(field_name)s header requires the OPTIONS method."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/cors.py:151
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `%(field_name)s` header is only used in a Cross-Origin Resource "
"Sharing (CORS) preflight\n"
"request.\n"
"\n"
"A preflight request uses the `OPTIONS` method; this request uses "
"`%(method)s`."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/cors.py:161
#, python-format
msgid "The %(field_name)s header requires the Origin header."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/cors.py:162
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `%(field_name)s` header is only used in a Cross-Origin Resource "
"Sharing (CORS) preflight\n"
"request.\n"
"\n"
"A preflight request requires the `Origin` header to be present."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/cors.py:172
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The %(field_name)s header requires the Access-Control-Request-Method "
"header."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/cors.py:173
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `%(field_name)s` header is only used in a Cross-Origin Resource "
"Sharing (CORS) preflight\n"
"request.\n"
"\n"
"A preflight request requires the `Access-Control-Request-Method` header "
"to be present."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/cors.py:183
msgid "This is a CORS preflight response."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/cors.py:184
msgid ""
"This is a Cross-Origin Resource Sharing (CORS) preflight response.\n"
"\n"
"It is a response to an `OPTIONS` request that includes an `Origin` and "
"`Access-Control-Request-Method`\n"
"header."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/cors.py:194
msgid "CORS headers are only allowed in preflight responses."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/cors.py:195
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The following header(s) are only used in the response to a Cross-Origin "
"Resource Sharing (CORS)\n"
"preflight request:\n"
"\n"
"%(headers)s\n"
"\n"
"A preflight request is an `OPTIONS` request that includes an `Origin` "
"header and an\n"
"`Access-Control-Request-Method` header.\n"
"\n"
"This response was not to a CORS preflight request, so these headers "
"should not be present."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/cors.py:210
msgid "Access-Control-Allow-Origin should not have multiple values."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/cors.py:211
msgid ""
"The `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` header can only contain a single "
"origin, `*`, or `null`. It\n"
"cannot contain a list of origins."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/cors.py:219
msgid "Access-Control-Allow-Credentials must be 'true'."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/cors.py:220
msgid ""
"The `Access-Control-Allow-Credentials` header must be set to `true` if "
"present. If you don't want\n"
"to allow credentials, omit the header."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/cors.py:228
msgid "The Access-Control-Allow-Origin header allows the requesting origin."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/cors.py:229
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` header matches the `Origin` header in "
"the request (`%(origin)s`).\n"
"\n"
"This means that the browser will let the requesting site access the "
"response."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/cors.py:238
msgid ""
"The Access-Control-Allow-Origin header does not allow the requesting "
"origin."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/cors.py:239
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` header (`%(acao_value)s`) does not "
"match the `Origin` header\n"
"in the request (`%(origin)s`).\n"
"\n"
"This means that the browser will **not** let the requesting site access "
"the response."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/cors.py:249
msgid "The Access-Control-Allow-Origin header does not allow any origin."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/cors.py:250
msgid ""
"The `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` header is set to `null`; this means "
"that no origin can access\n"
"the response."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/cors.py:258
msgid "The Access-Control-Allow-Origin header allows any origin."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/cors.py:259
msgid ""
"The `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` header is set to `*`; this means that "
"any origin can access\n"
"the response, unless the request includes credentials or requires a "
"preflight check."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/entity_tag.py:50
#, python-format
msgid "The %(field_name)s field's entity tag has a lower-case weak indicator."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/entity_tag.py:51
msgid ""
"An entity tag is weak when it starts with `W/`, and that prefix is case-"
"sensitive: a lower-case\n"
"`w/` isn't the weak indicator. Recipients can therefore treat the whole "
"value as an invalid tag,\n"
"or as a strong tag that happens to start with `w/`.\n"
"\n"
"See [the HTTP specification](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9110.html"
"#name-etag) for more\n"
"information."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/entity_tag.py:63
#, python-format
msgid "The %(field_name)s field mixes `*` with entity tags."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/entity_tag.py:64
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `*` in the `%(field_name)s` field matches any current representation,"
" so it is only valid\n"
"on its own: the field's value is either `*` or a list of entity tags\n"
"([RFC 9110, Section 13.1.1](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9110.html"
"#name-if-match) and\n"
"[Section 13.1.2](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9110.html#name-if-"
"none-match)).\n"
"\n"
"Recipients may handle a list that includes both in different ways; send "
"either `*` or the\n"
"entity tags."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/http_date.py:65
#, python-format
msgid "The %(field_name)s header's value isn't a valid date."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/http_date.py:66
msgid ""
"HTTP dates have specific syntax, and sending an invalid date can cause a "
"number of problems,\n"
"especially with caching. Common problems include sending \"1 May\" "
"instead of \"01 May\" (the month\n"
"is a fixed-width field), and sending a date in a timezone other than GMT."
"\n"
"\n"
"See [the HTTP specification](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9110.html"
"#name-date-time-formats) for more\n"
"information."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/http_date.py:78
#, python-format
msgid "The %(field_name)s header's value uses an obsolete format."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/http_date.py:79
msgid ""
"HTTP has a number of defined date formats for historical reasons. This "
"header is using an old\n"
"format that are now obsolete. See [the\n"
"specification](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9110.html#name-obsolete-"
"date-formats) for more information.\n"
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/json_field.py:78
#, python-format
msgid "The %(field_name)s header value isn't valid JSON."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/json_field.py:79
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Each `%(field_name)s` field line must be valid JSON.\n"
"\n"
"The JSON parsing error was:\n"
"    %(error)s"
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/media_type.py:143
#, python-format
msgid "The %(field_name)s field's media type name isn't registrable."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/media_type.py:144
#, python-format
msgid ""
"[RFC6838](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6838.html#section-4.2) "
"requires the type and\n"
"subtype names in a media type to start with a letter or a digit, and to "
"use only letters,\n"
"digits and the characters `!`, `#`, `$`, `&`, `-`, `^`, `_`, `.` and `+`."
" `%(value)s`\n"
"uses something else.\n"
"\n"
"HTTP's own syntax for media types is more permissive, so recipients are "
"likely to accept\n"
"this; however, a media type named this way can't be registered with IANA."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/media_type.py:157
#, python-format
msgid "The %(field_name)s field's media type name is too long."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/media_type.py:158
#, python-format
msgid ""
"[RFC6838](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6838.html#section-4.2) limits"
" the type and\n"
"subtype names in a media type to 127 characters each; `%(value)s` is "
"longer than that.\n"
"\n"
"It also recommends keeping them to 64 characters, because longer names "
"run into\n"
"implementation limits."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/params.py:208
#, python-format
msgid "The '%(param)s' parameter repeats in the %(field_name)s header."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/params.py:209
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Parameters on the `%(field_name)s` field should not repeat; "
"implementations may handle them\n"
"differently. Where a specification says, it's the first instance that "
"counts -- for example,\n"
"[RFC 8288](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8288.html#section-3.3) for "
"`Link`, and the\n"
"[Server Timing](https://w3c.github.io/server-timing/#the-server-timing-"
"header-field)\n"
"specification -- and that is the one used here."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/params.py:220
#, python-format
msgid "The '%(param)s' parameter on the %(field_name)s header is single-quoted."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/params.py:221
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `%(param)s`'s value on the `%(field_name)s` field starts and ends "
"with a single quote (').\n"
"However, single quotes don't mean anything there.\n"
"\n"
"This means that the value will be interpreted as `%(param_val)s`, **not**"
"\n"
"`%(param_val_unquoted)s`. If you intend the latter, remove the single "
"quotes."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/params.py:232
#, python-format
msgid "The %(param)s* parameter isn't allowed on the %(field_name)s field."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/params.py:233
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Parameters whose names end in '*' are reserved for non-ascii text, as "
"explained in\n"
"[RFC8187](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8187#section-4).\n"
"\n"
"The `%(param)s` parameter on the `%(field_name)s` field does not allow "
"this; you should use\n"
"%(param)s without the \"*\" on the end (and without the associated "
"encoding)."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/params.py:244
#, python-format
msgid "The '%(param)s' parameter's value cannot be quoted."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/params.py:245
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Parameters whose names end in '*' have values with a specific format, "
"defined in\n"
"[RFC8187](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8187#section-3.2.1), to allow"
" non-ASCII text.\n"
"\n"
"The `%(param)s` parameter on the `%(field_name)s` field has double-quotes"
" around it, which is not\n"
"valid."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/params.py:256
#, python-format
msgid "The %(param)s parameter's value is invalid."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/params.py:257
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Parameters whose names end in '*' have values with a specific format, "
"defined in\n"
"[RFC8187](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8187#section-3.2.1), to allow"
" non-ASCII text.\n"
"\n"
"The `%(param)s` parameter on the `%(field_name)s` field is not valid; it "
"needs to have three\n"
"parts, separated by single quotes (')."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/params.py:268
#, python-format
msgid "The %(param)s parameter's value doesn't define an encoding."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/params.py:269
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Parameters whose names end in '*' have values with a specific format, "
"defined in\n"
"[RFC8187](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8187#section-3.2.1), to allow"
" non-ASCII text.\n"
"\n"
"The `%(param)s` parameter on the `%(field_name)s` header doesn't declare "
"its character encoding,\n"
"which means that recipients can't understand it. It should be `UTF-8`."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/params.py:280
#, python-format
msgid "The %(param)s parameter's value uses an encoding other than UTF-8."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/params.py:281
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Parameters whose names end in '*' have values with a specific format, "
"defined in\n"
"[RFC8187](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8187#section-3.2.1), to allow"
" non-ASCII text.\n"
"\n"
"The `%(param)s` parameter on the `%(field_name)s` header uses the "
"`'%(enc)s` encoding, which has\n"
"interoperability issues with some browsers. It should be `UTF-8`."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/section.py:114
#, python-format
msgid "The %(field_name)s field is very large (%(field_size)s bytes)."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/section.py:115
msgid "Some implementations limit the size of any single field line."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/section.py:122
#, python-format
msgid "The %(field_type)s section is very large (%(section_size)s bytes)."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/section.py:123
msgid ""
"Some implementations limit the total size of a field section. 32KB is a "
"reasonable\n"
"upper limit."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/section.py:131
#, python-format
msgid "The %(field_name)s field's name contains non-ASCII characters."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/section.py:132
msgid "HTTP field names can only contain ASCII characters."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/section.py:139
#, python-format
msgid "The %(field_name)s field's name has whitespace around it."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/section.py:140
msgid ""
"HTTP field names can't be surrounded by whitespace; in particular, no "
"whitespace is allowed\n"
"between the field name and the colon. Recipients are required to reject "
"such messages, or to\n"
"remove the whitespace before processing the field. The whitespace has "
"been ignored here."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/section.py:149
#, python-format
msgid "The %(field_name)s field's value contains non-ASCII characters."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/section.py:150
msgid ""
"HTTP fields notionally use the ISO-8859-1 character set, but in most "
"cases are pure ASCII\n"
"(a subset of this encoding).\n"
"\n"
"This field has non-ASCII characters, which have been interpreted as being"
" encoded in\n"
"ISO-8859-1. If another encoding is used (e.g., UTF-8), the results may be"
" unpredictable."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/singleton_field.py:47
#, python-format
msgid "Only one %(field_name)s field is allowed in a message."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/singleton_field.py:48
msgid ""
"This field is designed to only occur once in a message. When it occurs "
"more than once, a receiver\n"
"needs to choose the one to use, which can lead to interoperability "
"problems, since different\n"
"implementations may make different choices."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/structured_field.py:86
#, python-format
msgid "In %(field_name)s, the %(context)s key '%(key)s' is duplicated."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/structured_field.py:87
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The %(context)s key '%(key)s' is duplicated. All instances after the "
"first will be ignored."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/structured_field.py:94
#, python-format
msgid "The %(field_name)s field value isn't a valid Structured Field."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/structured_field.py:95
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The %(field_name)s field is defined as a\n"
"[Structured Field](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9651.html),\n"
"but its value can't be parsed as one. As a result, this field is likely\n"
"to be ignored.\n"
"\n"
"The parser reports this error: `%(problem)s`\n"
"\n"
"%(context)s"
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/token_policy_field.py:77
#, python-format
msgid "The report-to parameter in %(field_name)s isn't a String%(report_only)s."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/token_policy_field.py:78
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `report-to` parameter in the `%(field_name)s` header names a "
"reporting endpoint, and has to be\n"
"a String (for example, `report-to=\"endpoint\"`). Browsers may ignore the"
" parameter when it is a\n"
"Token (`report-to=endpoint`) or any other type."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/unnecessary.py:45
#, python-format
msgid "The %(header_name)s header can probably be removed."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/unnecessary.py:46
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `%(header_name)s` header adds little value, contributes to "
"unnecessary bandwidth,\n"
"and may increase security risk by exposing details of the back-end "
"system.\n"
"\n"
"Consider removing it."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/accept.py:58
msgid "The Accept header contains a value that is not a media range."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/accept.py:59
#, python-format
msgid ""
"`%(value)s` is not a valid media range. `Accept` is a list of media "
"ranges\n"
"(e.g., `text/html`, `image/*`, `*/*`) that the client prefers in the "
"response;\n"
"see [its definition](%(ref_uri)s) for more information.%(position)s"
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/accept_ch.py:70
msgid "Accept-CH is ignored over plain HTTP."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/accept_ch.py:71
msgid ""
"The `Accept-CH` header field should only be used on secure (HTTPS) "
"responses. Using it over plain\n"
"HTTP exposes the user's information to network observers. Because of "
"this, browsers will ignore the\n"
"header."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/accept_ch.py:80
msgid "Accept-CH lists fields that are missing from Vary."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/accept_ch.py:81
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The following fields appear in `Accept-CH` but are not listed in the "
"`Vary` header:\n"
"`%(missing_fields)s`, even though the response is cacheable.\n"
"\n"
"Because these fields can affect the response content, they should be "
"included in `Vary` to ensure\n"
"that caches store separate responses for different client hints."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/accept_ch.py:92
msgid "The Accept-CH header isn't a List of Tokens."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/accept_ch.py:93
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The value for this field is legally formatted as a\n"
"[Structured Field](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8941.html), but it "
"isn't a list of Tokens.\n"
"As a result, it will likely be ignored by browsers.\n"
"\n"
"See [its definition](%(ref_uri)s) for more information."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/accept_language.py:75
msgid "The Accept-Language header isn't valid."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/accept_language.py:76
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The value for this field doesn't conform to its specified syntax; see "
"[its\n"
"definition](%(ref_uri)s) for more information.%(position)s"
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/accept_patch.py:33
msgid "The Accept-Patch header contains a value that is not a media type."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/accept_patch.py:34
#, python-format
msgid ""
"`%(value)s` is not a valid media type. `Accept-Patch` is a list of media "
"types\n"
"(e.g., `application/json-patch+json`) accepted in a PATCH request; see "
"[its\n"
"definition](%(ref_uri)s) for more information.%(position)s"
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/accept_post.py:36
msgid "The Accept-Post header contains a value that is not a media type."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/accept_post.py:37
#, python-format
msgid ""
"`%(value)s` is not a valid media type. `Accept-Post` is a list of media "
"types\n"
"(e.g., `text/turtle`) accepted in a POST request; see [its "
"definition](%(ref_uri)s)\n"
"for more information.%(position)s"
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/accept_query.py:58
msgid "The Accept-Query header contains a value that isn't a media range."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/accept_query.py:59
#, python-format
msgid ""
"`Accept-Query` is a List Structured Field whose members are Tokens or "
"Strings, each\n"
"naming a media range accepted in the content of a QUERY request. "
"`%(value)s` is\n"
"neither, so it will be ignored."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/accept_query.py:68
msgid "The Accept-Query header contains a value that is not a media range."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/accept_query.py:69
#, python-format
msgid ""
"`%(value)s` is not a valid media range. `Accept-Query` is a list of media"
" ranges\n"
"(e.g., `application/sparql-query`, `text/*`) accepted in the content of a"
" QUERY\n"
"request; see [its definition](%(ref_uri)s) for more information."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/accept_ranges.py:32
msgid "This response advertises support for non-standard range-units."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/accept_ranges.py:33
msgid ""
"The `Accept-Ranges` response header tells clients what `range-unit`s a "
"resource is willing to\n"
"process in future requests. HTTP only defines two: `bytes` and `none`.\n"
"\n"
"Clients who don't know about the non-standard range-unit will not be able"
" to use it."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/access_control_max_age.py:43
msgid "Access-Control-Max-Age must be an integer."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/access_control_max_age.py:44
msgid ""
"The `Access-Control-Max-Age` header indicates how many seconds a "
"preflight response can be cached\n"
"for. It must be a non-negative integer."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/access_control_max_age.py:52
msgid "Access-Control-Max-Age must be non-negative."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/access_control_max_age.py:53
msgid ""
"The `Access-Control-Max-Age` header indicates how many seconds a "
"preflight response can be cached\n"
"for. It cannot be less than zero."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/age.py:44
msgid "The Age header's value should be an integer."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/age.py:45
msgid ""
"The `Age` header indicates the age of the response; i.e., how long it has"
" been cached\n"
"since it was generated. The value given was not an integer, so it is not "
"a valid age."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/age.py:53
msgid "The Age headers' value must be a positive integer."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/age.py:54
msgid ""
"The `Age` header indicates the age of the response; i.e., how long it has"
" been cached\n"
"since it was generated. The value given was negative, so it is not a "
"valid age."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/age.py:62
msgid "The Age header's value is very large."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/age.py:63
msgid ""
"The `Age` header's value is greater than 2,147,483,648. Some "
"implementations may represent it\n"
"using that value (which is over 68 years).\n"
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/alt_svc.py:51
msgid "The Alt-Svc 'clear' token cannot be used with other values."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/alt_svc.py:52
msgid ""
"The `Alt-Svc` header field value \"clear\" is used to invalidate previous"
" alternative services.\n"
"It cannot be combined with other alternative service advertisements."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/available_dictionary.py:45
msgid ""
"This request's dictionary can't be used, because Accept-Encoding doesn't "
"list dcb or dcz as acceptable."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/available_dictionary.py:49
msgid ""
"The `Available-Dictionary` header is present, but `Accept-Encoding` "
"doesn't list `dcb` or `dcz` as\n"
"acceptable: it leaves them out, or gives them a `q` value of 0. (A `*` "
"isn't counted.) A server\n"
"therefore can't use the dictionary to compress the response.\n"
"\n"
"[RFC 9842 Section 6.1](https://www.rfc-"
"editor.org/rfc/rfc9842.html#section-6.1) describes how a\n"
"client advertises the dictionary-aware content encodings that it "
"supports, by adding them to\n"
"`Accept-Encoding`."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/available_dictionary.py:62
msgid "The Available-Dictionary header has an invalid type."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/available_dictionary.py:63
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `Available-Dictionary` header value must be a Byte Sequence. Found "
"`%(got)s`."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cache_control.py:251
#, python-format
msgid "The %(directive)s cache directive does not accept a value."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cache_control.py:252
#, python-format
msgid "The `%(directive)s` cache directive is a flag; it shouldn't have a value."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cache_control.py:258
#, python-format
msgid "The %(directive)s cache directive's value is incorrect."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cache_control.py:259
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `%(directive)s` cache directive type is %(expected_type)s, but "
"`%(value)s` was found."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cache_control.py:268
#, python-format
msgid "The %(directive)s cache directive requires a value."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cache_control.py:269
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `%(directive)s` cache directive requires a value (a non-negative "
"integer), but none was given."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cache_control.py:278
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The %(directive)s cache directive's value is quoted but should be a bare "
"number."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cache_control.py:279
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `%(directive)s` cache directive's value is a number, so senders must "
"not generate it as a\n"
"quoted string. [RFC 9111](https://www.rfc-"
"editor.org/rfc/rfc9111.html#section-5.2) says that\n"
"recipients ought to accept both forms, so it has been interpreted as if "
"it were not quoted, but\n"
"some implementations may not recognise the quoted form."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cache_control.py:289
#, python-format
msgid "The %(directive)s cache directive is very large."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cache_control.py:290
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `%(directive)s` cache directive's value is greater than 2^31-1. Some "
"implementations may not be\n"
"able to handle values this large."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cache_control.py:298
#, python-format
msgid "The %(directive)s cache directive has non-lowercase characters."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cache_control.py:299
#, python-format
msgid ""
"cache directive names are case-insensitive, but some implementations "
"don't\n"
"recognize directives that aren't all-lowercase.\n"
"\n"
"Therefore, it's safest to use `%(directive_lower)s` instead of "
"`%(directive)s`."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cache_control.py:309
#, python-format
msgid "The %(directive)s cache directive appears more than once."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cache_control.py:310
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `%(directive)s` cache directive is only defined to appear once; it is"
" used more than\n"
"once here, so implementations may use different instances (e.g., the "
"first, or the last),\n"
"making their behaviour unpredictable."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cache_control.py:319
#, python-format
msgid "The %(directive)s cache directive overrides other directives."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cache_control.py:320
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `%(directive)s` cache directive overrides or conflicts with these "
"other directives: \n"
"\n"
"%(conflicts)s\n"
"\n"
"The conflicting directives will be ignored by caches, and can be safely "
"omitted.\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cache_control.py:332
#, python-format
msgid "The %(directive)s cache directive has no meaning in a %(message_type)s."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cache_control.py:333
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `%(directive)s` cache directive is only defined to appear in "
"%(other_message)s\n"
"messages; is has no defined meaning in a %(message_type)s."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cache_control.py:341
msgid "Only one of the pre-check and post-check cache directives is present."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cache_control.py:344
msgid ""
"Microsoft Internet Explorer implements two `Cache-Control` extensions, "
"`pre-check` and\n"
"`post-check`, to give more control over how its cache stores responses.\n"
"\n"
"This response uses only one of these directives; as a result, Internet "
"Explorer will ignore the\n"
"directive, since it requires both to be present.\n"
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cache_control.py:356
msgid "The pre-check and post-check cache directives are both '0'."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cache_control.py:359
msgid ""
"Microsoft Internet Explorer implements two `Cache-Control` extensions, "
"`pre-check` and\n"
"`post-check`, to give more control over how its cache stores responses.\n"
"\n"
"This response gives a value of \"0\" for both; as a result, Internet "
"Explorer will ignore the\n"
"directive, since it requires both to be present.\n"
"\n"
"In other words, setting these to zero has **no effect** (besides wasting "
"bandwidth),\n"
"and may trigger bugs in some beta versions of IE."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cache_control.py:373
msgid "The post-check cache directive's value is larger than pre-check's."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cache_control.py:376
msgid ""
"Microsoft Internet Explorer implements two `Cache-Control` extensions, "
"`pre-check` and\n"
"`post-check`, to give more control over how its cache stores responses.\n"
"\n"
"This response assigns a higher value to `post-check` than to `pre-check`;"
" this means that Internet\n"
"Explorer will treat `post-check` as if its value is the same as `pre-"
"check`'s."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cache_control.py:387
msgid "The post-check cache directive's value is '0'."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cache_control.py:390
msgid ""
"Microsoft Internet Explorer implements two `Cache-Control` extensions, "
"`pre-check` and\n"
"`post-check`, to give more control over how its cache stores responses.\n"
"\n"
"This response assigns a value of \"0\" to `post-check`, which means that "
"Internet Explorer will reload\n"
"the content as soon as it enters the browser cache, effectively "
"**doubling the load on the\n"
"server**."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cache_control.py:402
msgid "This response may be refreshed in the background by Internet Explorer."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cache_control.py:405
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Microsoft Internet Explorer implements two `Cache-Control` extensions, "
"`pre-check` and\n"
"`post-check`, to give more control over how its cache stores responses.\n"
"\n"
"Once it has been cached for more than %(post_check)s seconds, a new "
"request will result in the\n"
"cached response being served while it is refreshed in the background. "
"However, if it has been\n"
"cached for more than %(pre_check)s seconds, the browser will download a "
"fresh response before\n"
"showing it to the user.\n"
"\n"
"Note that these directives do not have any effect on other clients or "
"caches."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cache_group_invalidation.py:49
#: httplint/field/parsers/cache_groups.py:42
msgid "Cache groups need to be strings."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cache_group_invalidation.py:50
#: httplint/field/parsers/cache_groups.py:43
#, python-format
msgid "The `%(field_name)s` header values must be Strings. Found `%(got)s`."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cache_group_invalidation.py:57
#, python-format
msgid "The Cache-Group-Invalidation header is ignored for %(method)s requests."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cache_group_invalidation.py:58
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `Cache-Group-Invalidation` header is only processed for unsafe "
"methods (like POST, PUT, DELETE).\n"
"It will be ignored for `%(method)s` requests."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cache_status.py:108
msgid "Detailed information about caching is available."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cache_status.py:109
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `Cache-Status` header field indicates how caches have handled the "
"response.\n"
"\n"
"%(status)s\n"
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cache_status.py:119
#, python-format
msgid "A Cache-Status member is %(member_type)s, not a String or Token."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cache_status.py:120
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Each member of the `Cache-Status` list identifies the cache that inserted"
" it, and\n"
"[RFC 9211](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9211.html#section-2) "
"requires it to be a String or\n"
"a Token. This member, `%(value)s`, is %(member_type)s."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cache_status.py:129
#, python-format
msgid "The Cache-Status header has an unknown parameter '%(param)s'."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cache_status.py:130
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `%(param)s` parameter is not defined in the Cache-Status "
"specification.\n"
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cache_status.py:138
#, python-format
msgid "The Cache-Status header has an unknown value for '%(param)s'."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cache_status.py:139
#: httplint/field/parsers/proxy_status.py:156
#, python-format
msgid "The value `%(value)s` is not defined for the `%(param)s` parameter.\n"
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cdn_cache_control.py:77
#, python-format
msgid "The %(bad_directive)s CDN cache directive's value is incorrect."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cdn_cache_control.py:78
#, python-format
msgid "The value for this directive must be %(expected_type)s."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cdn_cache_control.py:84
msgid "This response targets cache directives to Content Delivery Networks."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cdn_cache_control.py:85
msgid ""
"The `CDN-Cache-Control` header field allows you to specify cache "
"directives that are targeted at\n"
"Content Delivery Network (CDN) caches, separately from the `Cache-"
"Control` header field (which\n"
"applies to all caches)."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/clear_site_data.py:62
msgid "This response clears browser-side data for this origin."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/clear_site_data.py:63
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `Clear-Site-Data` header instructs the browser to clear the following"
" data for this origin:\n"
"%(values)s.\n"
"\n"
"This is useful for actions such as logout, account switching, or session "
"termination, where\n"
"locally-stored data should not persist."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/clear_site_data.py:74
#, python-format
msgid "The Clear-Site-Data header contains an unknown value '%(value)s'."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/clear_site_data.py:75
msgid ""
"The `Clear-Site-Data` header contains a value that is not recognized.\n"
"Valid values are: `\"cache\"`, `\"cookies\"`, `\"storage\"`, "
"`\"executionContexts\"`, `\"*\"`."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/clear_site_data.py:83
msgid "The Clear-Site-Data header has an empty value."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/clear_site_data.py:84
msgid ""
"The `Clear-Site-Data` header value is empty. It should contain at least "
"one directive."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/clear_site_data.py:91
msgid "Clear-Site-Data contains unquoted values."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/clear_site_data.py:92
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Values in the `Clear-Site-Data` header must be quoted; unquoted values "
"will be ignored. \n"
"\n"
"The following values were found unquoted: `%(values)s`."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_disposition.py:47
#, python-format
msgid "The '%(disposition)s' Content-Disposition isn't known."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_disposition.py:48
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `Content-Disposition` header has two widely-known values; `inline` "
"and `attachment`.\n"
"`%(disposition)s` isn't recognised, and most implementations will default"
" to handling it like\n"
"`attachment`."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_disposition.py:57
msgid "The Content-Disposition header doesn't have a 'filename' parameter."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_disposition.py:58
msgid ""
"The `Content-Disposition` header with a disposition of `attachment` "
"suggests a filename for clients\n"
"to use when saving the file locally.\n"
"\n"
"It should always contain a `filename` parameter, even when the "
"`filename*` parameter is used to\n"
"carry an internationalised filename, so that browsers can fall back to an"
" ASCII-only filename."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_disposition.py:69
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The 'filename' parameter on the Content-Disposition header contains a "
"'%%' character."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_disposition.py:72
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `Content-Disposition` header suggests a filename for clients to use "
"when saving the file\n"
"locally, using the `filename` parameter.\n"
"\n"
"[RFC6266](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6266) specifies how to carry "
"non-ASCII characters in this\n"
"parameter. However, historically some (but not all) browsers have also "
"decoded %%-encoded\n"
"characters in the `filename` parameter, which means that they'll be "
"treated differently depending\n"
"on the browser you're using.\n"
"\n"
"As a result, it's not interoperable to use percent characters in the "
"`filename` parameter. Use the\n"
"correct encoding in the `filename*` parameter instead."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_disposition.py:88
msgid "The filename in the Content-Disposition header contains a path character."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_disposition.py:89
msgid ""
"The `Content-Disposition` header suggests a filename for clients to use "
"when saving the file\n"
"locally, using the `filename` and `filename*` parameters.\n"
"\n"
"One of these parameters contains a path character (\"\\\" or \"/\"), used"
" to navigate between\n"
"directories on common operating systems.\n"
"\n"
"Because this can be used to attach the browser's host operating system "
"(e.g., by saving a file to a\n"
"system directory), browsers will usually ignore these parameters, or "
"remove path information.\n"
"\n"
"You should remove these characters."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_encoding.py:69
msgid ""
"This response is compressed with a dictionary,but is missing Vary: "
"Available-Dictionary."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_encoding.py:73
msgid ""
"The response is compressed with a dictionary (dcb or dcz) and is "
"cacheable, but does not list\n"
"`Available-Dictionary` in the `Vary` header.\n"
"\n"
"[RFC 9842 Section 6.2](https://www.rfc-"
"editor.org/rfc/rfc9842.html#section-6.2) requires that\n"
"cacheable dictionary-compressed responses MUST include `Available-"
"Dictionary` in the `Vary` header\n"
"to prevent serving compressed content to clients that do not have the "
"dictionary."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_encoding.py:85
#, python-format
msgid ""
"This response uses the '%(coding)s' content-coding, but it wasn't "
"requested."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_encoding.py:86
#, python-format
msgid ""
"This response's `Content-Encoding` header indicates it has the "
"`%(coding)s` content-coding\n"
"applied, but the client didn't ask for it in the request: either it "
"didn't list the coding\n"
"(or `*`) in `Accept-Encoding`, or it gave the coding a `q` value of 0 to "
"refuse it.\n"
"\n"
"Normally, clients ask for the encodings they want in the `Accept-"
"Encoding` request header. Using\n"
"encodings that the client doesn't explicitly request can lead to "
"interoperability problems."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_language.py:42
#, python-format
msgid "The %(lang)s language tag appears more than once."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_language.py:43
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `%(lang)s` language tag is used more than once in the `Content-"
"Language` header.\n"
"\n"
"Recipients will likely ignore duplicates."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_length.py:46
msgid "Content-Length should be an integer."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_length.py:47
msgid "The `Content-Length` header should be an integer, but it was not."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_length.py:54
msgid "Content-Length and Transfer-Encoding should not be present together."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_length.py:55
msgid ""
"RFC 9110 Section 8.6:\n"
"> A sender MUST NOT send a Content-Length header field in any message "
"that contains a Transfer-Encoding header field.\n"
"\n"
"This is because `Transfer-Encoding` overrides `Content-Length`."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_length.py:65
msgid "The Content-Length header is very large."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_length.py:66
msgid ""
"The `Content-Length` header's value is greater than 2^63-1. Some "
"implementations may not be able to\n"
"handle values this large."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_range.py:175
msgid "This response shouldn't have a Content-Range header."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_range.py:176
msgid ""
"HTTP only defines meaning for the `Content-Range` header in responses "
"with a `206` (Partial\n"
"Content) or `416` (Requested Range Not Satisfiable) status code.\n"
"\n"
"Because the status code is neither of those, this `Content-Range` header "
"may confuse caches and\n"
"clients."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_range.py:187
msgid "The Content-Range header is missing a unit (e.g., 'bytes')."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_range.py:188
msgid ""
"The `Content-Range` header is missing a range unit at the start; it "
"should\n"
"almost always be `bytes`.\n"
"\n"
"For example:\n"
"\n"
"    Content-Range: bytes 1-100/200\n"
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_range.py:201
msgid "The Content-Range header invalidly uses wildcards."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_range.py:202
msgid ""
"The `Content-Range` header cannot use a wildcard (`*`) for both the range"
" and the complete length.\n"
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_range.py:210
msgid "The Content-Range header is missing a slash separator."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_range.py:211
msgid ""
"The `Content-Range` header is missing a slash (`/`) separating the range "
"from the complete length.\n"
"\n"
"For example:\n"
"\n"
"    Content-Range: bytes 1-100/200\n"
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_range.py:223
msgid "The Content-Range header is missing a hyphen."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_range.py:224
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The range specifier `%(value)s` is missing a hyphen separating the start "
"and end positions."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_range.py:231
msgid "The Content-Range header contains a non-integer value."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_range.py:232
#, python-format
msgid "The value `%(value)s` is not a valid integer."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_range.py:239
msgid "The Content-Range header contains an integer with too many digits."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_range.py:240
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The value `%(value)s` has more than %(max_digits)s digits, which is more "
"than recipients can be\n"
"expected to handle."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_range.py:248
msgid "The Content-Range header is invalid."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_range.py:249
msgid ""
"The values indicated by the `Content-Range` header are not valid. The "
"first position must be less\n"
"than or equal to the last position, and the last position must be less "
"than the complete length."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_range.py:257
msgid ""
"The Content-Range header indicates an unsatisfied range, but the status "
"code is 206."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_range.py:260
msgid ""
"The `Content-Range` header uses the `*/<length>` syntax, which is "
"reserved for `416` (Requested\n"
"Range Not Satisfiable) responses to indicate the actual length of the "
"resource.\n"
"\n"
"The `206` response status code indicates a successful range response, so "
"this header is\n"
"incorrect."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_range.py:271
msgid "A 416 response should use the unsatisfied-range form of Content-Range."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_range.py:272
msgid ""
"When a `416` (Range Not Satisfiable) response includes a `Content-Range` "
"header, it should use\n"
"the `bytes */<length>` form, which tells the client how long the "
"representation currently is.\n"
"\n"
"This response uses a range that was satisfied (like `bytes 1-100/200`), "
"which is how a `206`\n"
"(Partial Content) response is described, so clients may not know why "
"their range failed."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_range.py:283
msgid "The Content-Range header indicates an unknown total length."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_range.py:284
msgid ""
"The `Content-Range` header uses `*` for the instance length, indicating "
"that the total length of\n"
"the resource is unknown."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_security_policy.py:202
#, python-format
msgid "This response sets a Content Security Policy%(report_only)s."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_security_policy.py:203
#, python-format
msgid ""
"[Content Security Policy](https://www.w3.org/TR/CSP3/) allows the server "
"to declare\n"
"the sources of content that browsers are allowed to use on a "
"page.%(report_only_text)s"
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_security_policy.py:211
msgid "Inline scripts are allowed."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_security_policy.py:212
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `'unsafe-inline'` [Content Security "
"Policy](https://www.w3.org/TR/CSP3/)\n"
"directive allows the execution of inline scripts and event handlers, "
"which\n"
"significantly reduces the protection provided by CSP against Cross-Site\n"
"Scripting (XSS) attacks.\n"
"\n"
"It was found in the following directives:\n"
"\n"
"%(directives_list)s"
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_security_policy.py:226
msgid "Unsafe script evaluation is allowed."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_security_policy.py:227
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `'unsafe-eval'` [Content Security "
"Policy](https://www.w3.org/TR/CSP3/)\n"
"directive allows the use of string-to-code mechanisms like `eval()`, "
"which can make it easier for\n"
"attackers to execute malicious code.\n"
"\n"
"It was found in the following directives:\n"
"\n"
"%(directives_list)s"
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_security_policy.py:240
msgid "Loading from insecure HTTP sources is allowed."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_security_policy.py:241
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Allowing `http:` sources in `%(field_name)s` can allow attackers to "
"intercept and modify\n"
"content loaded by the page, potentially bypassing security controls.\n"
"\n"
"It was found in the following directives:\n"
"\n"
"%(directives_list)s"
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_security_policy.py:253
msgid "Duplicate directives are present."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_security_policy.py:254
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Directives must only appear once in the `%(field_name)s` header; "
"subsequent occurrences are ignored.\n"
"\n"
"The following directives were duplicated:\n"
"\n"
"%(directives_list)s"
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_security_policy.py:265
msgid "The deprecated report-uri directive is used."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_security_policy.py:266
msgid ""
"The `report-uri` [Content Security Policy](https://www.w3.org/TR/CSP3/)\n"
"directive is deprecated in favor of `report-to`. It is recommended to use"
" `report-to`\n"
"for reporting violations, although `report-uri` may still be supported "
"for backward\n"
"compatibility."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_security_policy.py:276
msgid "All sources are allowed in one or more directives."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_security_policy.py:277
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `*` [Content Security Policy](https://www.w3.org/TR/CSP3/)\n"
"directive allows resources to be loaded from any origin, which "
"significantly reduces the protection\n"
"provided by CSP.%(report_only_text)s\n"
"\n"
"It was found in the following directives:\n"
"\n"
"%(directives_list)s"
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_security_policy.py:290
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The report-to name '%(endpoint)s' doesn't match a Reporting-Endpoints "
"entry."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_security_policy.py:291
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `report-to` directive in [Content Security "
"Policy](https://www.w3.org/TR/CSP3/)\n"
"names a reporting endpoint. The Reporting API matches that name against "
"the entries in the\n"
"`Reporting-Endpoints` header, and none has this name.\n"
"\n"
"The specification does not use legacy `Report-To` groups for this, so a "
"group with this name in a\n"
"`Report-To` header does not satisfy it.%(report_only_text)s"
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_type.py:55
#, python-format
msgid "The '%(charset)s' character encoding isn't one that recipients recognise."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_type.py:56
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `charset` parameter on the `%(field_name)s` field is `%(charset)s`, "
"which isn't a label in the\n"
"[Encoding Standard](https://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/#names-and-labels). "
"Browsers and other\n"
"recipients that follow it will ignore the parameter, and guess the "
"encoding or use a default.\n"
"\n"
"It might still be a valid name; the\n"
"[IANA registry](https://www.iana.org/assignments/character-sets) includes"
" encodings such as\n"
"`UTF-7` and `UTF-32` that browsers don't support. Either way, it's "
"unlikely to interoperate.\n"
"Consider `utf-8`."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_type.py:70
#, python-format
msgid "The '%(charset)s' character encoding is blocked by browsers."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_type.py:71
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `charset` parameter on the `%(field_name)s` field is `%(charset)s`. "
"The\n"
"[Encoding Standard](https://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/#names-and-labels) "
"maps this label to its\n"
"`replacement` encoding, which browsers don't decode; it does so because "
"encodings like this one\n"
"can be used to inject crafted content.\n"
"\n"
"Use an encoding that browsers support, such as `utf-8`."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_type.py:83
#, python-format
msgid "The '%(charset)s' character encoding isn't a registered name."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/content_type.py:84
#, python-format
msgid ""
"[RFC 9110](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9110.html#name-charset) says"
" that charset names\n"
"ought to be registered in the [IANA "
"registry](https://www.iana.org/assignments/character-sets).\n"
"`%(charset)s` isn't in it.\n"
"\n"
"Browsers recognise it, and treat it as `%(encoding)s`, but recipients "
"that rely on the registry\n"
"might not. Use a registered name; for UTF-8, that's `utf-8`."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cross_origin_embedder_policy.py:18
#, python-format
msgid "This response requires resources to have a CORP header%(report_only)s."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cross_origin_embedder_policy.py:19
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `require-corp`\n"
"[Cross Origin Embedder Policy](https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#cross-"
"origin-embedder-policy-header)\n"
"requires that all cross-origin resources must explicitly grant permission"
" to be loaded via a\n"
"`Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy` header, in supporting "
"browsers.%(report_only_text)s"
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cross_origin_embedder_policy.py:29
#, python-format
msgid ""
"This response loads cross-origin resources without "
"credentials%(report_only)s."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cross_origin_embedder_policy.py:30
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `credentialless`\n"
"[Cross-Origin Embedder Policy](https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#cross-"
"origin-embedder-policy-header)\n"
"allows loading cross-origin resources without explicit permission in "
"supporting browsers, but\n"
"requests for them will not include credentials (cookies, client "
"certificates,\n"
"etc.).%(report_only_text)s"
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cross_origin_embedder_policy.py:41
#, python-format
msgid ""
"This response allows loading cross-origin resources without "
"restriction%(report_only)s."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cross_origin_embedder_policy.py:44
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `unsafe-none`\n"
"[Cross-Origin Embedder Policy](https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#cross-"
"origin-embedder-policy-header)\n"
"is the default behavior, allowing cross-origin resources to be loaded\n"
"without explicit permission in supporting browsers.\n"
"\n"
"This does not provide cross-origin isolation.%(report_only_text)s"
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cross_origin_embedder_policy.py:56
#: httplint/field/parsers/cross_origin_opener_policy.py:68
#, python-format
msgid "This response's %(field_name)s has an invalid value."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cross_origin_embedder_policy.py:57
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `%(field_name)s` header must be one of `require-corp`, "
"`credentialless`, or\n"
"`unsafe-none`.\n"
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cross_origin_embedder_policy.py:66
#: httplint/field/parsers/cross_origin_opener_policy.py:78
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The report-to name '%(endpoint)s' doesn't match a Reporting-Endpoints "
"entry%(report_only)s."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cross_origin_embedder_policy.py:70
msgid ""
"The `report-to` parameter in the\n"
"[Cross-Origin Embedder Policy](https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#cross-"
"origin-embedder-policy-header)\n"
"header names a reporting endpoint. The Reporting API matches that name "
"against the entries in the\n"
"`Reporting-Endpoints` header, and none has this name.\n"
"\n"
"The specification does not use legacy `Report-To` groups for this, so a "
"group with this name in a\n"
"`Report-To` header does not satisfy it."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cross_origin_embedder_policy_report_only.py:22
msgid "This response has both enforcing and report-only COEP headers."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cross_origin_embedder_policy_report_only.py:23
msgid ""
"A response should not have both `Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy` and\n"
"`Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy-Report-Only` headers. The report-only "
"header will be ignored."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cross_origin_opener_policy.py:18
#, python-format
msgid ""
"This response isolates the browsing context to the same "
"origin%(report_only)s."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cross_origin_opener_policy.py:19
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `same-origin`\n"
"[Cross-Origin Opener "
"Policy](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/origin.html#coop)\n"
"isolates the browsing context, preventing it from sharing a window object"
"\n"
"with cross-origin documents in supporting browsers.%(report_only_text)s"
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cross_origin_opener_policy.py:29
#, python-format
msgid ""
"This response isolates the browsing context but allows "
"popups%(report_only)s."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cross_origin_opener_policy.py:30
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `same-origin-allow-popups`\n"
"[Cross-Origin Opener "
"Policy](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/origin.html#coop)\n"
"isolates the browsing context but maintains a relationship\n"
"with popups that it opens, or that opened it, in supporting "
"browsers.%(report_only_text)s"
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cross_origin_opener_policy.py:40
#, python-format
msgid ""
"This response is always placed in a new browsing context "
"group%(report_only)s."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cross_origin_opener_policy.py:41
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `noopener-allow-popups`\n"
"[Cross-Origin Opener "
"Policy](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/origin.html#coop)\n"
"forces the document into a new top-level browsing context, severing any "
"opener\n"
"relationship with the document that opened it, in supporting browsers.\n"
"\n"
"As the HTML specification notes, this does not create a robust security "
"boundary between\n"
"those same-origin documents.%(report_only_text)s"
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cross_origin_opener_policy.py:54
#, python-format
msgid ""
"This response allows sharing the browsing context with cross-origin "
"documents%(report_only)s."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cross_origin_opener_policy.py:58
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `unsafe-none`\n"
"[Cross-Origin Opener "
"Policy](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/origin.html#coop)\n"
"is the default behavior in supporting browsers. It allows the document to"
" share a browsing context\n"
"group with other documents unless they enforce "
"isolation.%(report_only_text)s"
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cross_origin_opener_policy.py:69
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `%(field_name)s` header must be one of `same-origin`, `same-origin-"
"allow-popups`,\n"
"`noopener-allow-popups`, or `unsafe-none`.\n"
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cross_origin_opener_policy.py:82
msgid ""
"The `report-to` parameter in the\n"
"[Cross-Origin Opener "
"Policy](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/origin.html#coop)\n"
"header names a reporting endpoint. The Reporting API matches that name "
"against the entries in the\n"
"`Reporting-Endpoints` header, and none has this name.\n"
"\n"
"The specification does not use legacy `Report-To` groups for this, so a "
"group with this name in a\n"
"`Report-To` header does not satisfy it."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cross_origin_opener_policy_report_only.py:23
msgid "This response has both enforcing and report-only COOP headers."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cross_origin_opener_policy_report_only.py:24
msgid ""
"A response should not have both `Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy` and\n"
"`Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy-Report-Only` headers. The report-only header "
"will be ignored."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cross_origin_resource_policy.py:40
msgid ""
"This response is only available for reading to requests from the same "
"origin."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cross_origin_resource_policy.py:41
msgid ""
"The `same-origin`\n"
"[Cross-Origin Resource Policy](https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#cross-"
"origin-resource-policy-header)\n"
"prevents the resource from being read by any cross-origin document \n"
"in supporting browsers."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cross_origin_resource_policy.py:51
msgid "This response is available for reading to requests from the same site."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cross_origin_resource_policy.py:52
msgid ""
"The `same-site`\n"
"[Cross-Origin Resource Policy](https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#cross-"
"origin-resource-policy-header)\n"
"allows the resource to be read by documents from the same site, but\n"
"prevents it from being read by cross-site documents in supporting "
"browsers."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cross_origin_resource_policy.py:62
msgid "This response is available for reading to requests from all origins."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cross_origin_resource_policy.py:63
msgid ""
"The `cross-origin`\n"
"[Cross-Origin Resource Policy](https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#cross-"
"origin-resource-policy-header)\n"
"allows the resource to be read by any document in supporting browsers, "
"regardless of its \n"
"origin."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cross_origin_resource_policy.py:73
msgid "Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy has an invalid value."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/cross_origin_resource_policy.py:74
#, python-format
msgid ""
"`%(value)s` is not a valid in the `Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy` header;\n"
"it must be one of `same-origin`, `same-site`, or `cross-origin`.\n"
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/date.py:45
msgid "The server's clock is correct."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/date.py:46
msgid ""
"HTTP's caching model assumes reasonable synchronisation between clocks on"
" the server and client;\n"
"compared to the local clock, the server's clock appears to be well-"
"synchronised."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/date.py:54
#, python-format
msgid "The server's clock is %(clock_skew_string)s."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/date.py:55
msgid ""
"Compared to the local clock, the server's clock does not appear to be "
"well-synchronised.\n"
"\n"
"HTTP's caching model assumes reasonable synchronisation between clocks on"
" the server and client;\n"
"clock skew can cause responses that should be cacheable to be considered "
"uncacheable (especially if\n"
"their freshness lifetime is short).\n"
"\n"
"Ask your server administrator to synchronise the clock, e.g., using\n"
"[NTP](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Network_Time_Protocol \"Network Time "
"Protocol\").\n"
"\n"
"Apparent clock skew can also be caused by caching the response without "
"adjusting the `Age` header;\n"
"e.g., in a reverse proxy or Content Delivery network. See [this\n"
"paper](https://www.usenix.org/legacy/events/usits01/full_papers/cohen/cohen_html/index.html)"
" for more information. "
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/date.py:73
msgid "It appears that the Date header has been changed by an intermediary."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/date.py:74
msgid ""
"It appears that this response has been cached by a reverse proxy or "
"Content Delivery Network,\n"
"because the `Age` header is present, but the `Date` header is more recent"
" than it indicates.\n"
"\n"
"Generally, reverse proxies should either omit the `Age` header (if they "
"have another means of\n"
"determining how fresh the response is), or leave the `Date` header alone "
"(i.e., act as a normal\n"
"HTTP cache).\n"
"\n"
"See [this "
"paper](https://www.usenix.org/legacy/events/usits01/full_papers/cohen/cohen_html/index.html)"
"\n"
"for more information."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/deprecation.py:45
msgid "The resource has been deprecated."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/deprecation.py:46
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `Deprecation` header indicates that this resource was deprecated on "
"%(date)s."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/deprecation.py:53
msgid "The resource will be deprecated."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/deprecation.py:54
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `Deprecation` header indicates that this resource will be deprecated "
"on %(date)s."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/deprecation.py:61
msgid "The Deprecation header value is invalid."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/deprecation.py:62
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `Deprecation` [Structured Field](https://www.rfc-"
"editor.org/rfc/rfc8941.html)\n"
"header must be a Date. Found: %(item_type)s."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/expect.py:38
#, python-format
msgid "The '%(expectation)s' expectation is not supported."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/expect.py:39
msgid ""
"HTTP only defines one expectation, `100-continue`. This expectation is "
"not recognized."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/expect.py:46
msgid "The Expect header is not supported in HTTP/1.0."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/expect.py:47
msgid "The `Expect` header was added in HTTP/1.1; it has no meaning in HTTP/1.0."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/if_range.py:57
#, python-format
msgid "The %(field_name)s header's entity tag is weak."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/if_range.py:58
msgid ""
"[RFC 9110](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9110.html#name-if-range) "
"says that a client must\n"
"not send a weak entity tag in `If-Range`. Because the comparison it "
"requires is a strong one, a\n"
"server will never find a weak tag to match, so the whole representation "
"is sent instead of the\n"
"range requested."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/last_modified.py:42
msgid "The Last-Modified time is in the future."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/last_modified.py:43
msgid ""
"The `Last-Modified` header indicates the last point in time that the "
"resource has changed.\n"
"This response's `Last-Modified` time is in the future, which doesn't have"
" any defined meaning in\n"
"HTTP."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/last_modified.py:52
#, python-format
msgid "The resource last changed %(last_modified_string)s."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/last_modified.py:53
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `Last-Modified` header indicates the last point in time that the "
"resource has changed. It is\n"
"used in HTTP for validating cached responses, and for calculating "
"heuristic freshness in caches.\n"
"\n"
"This resource last changed %(last_modified_string)s."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/link.py:143
#, python-format
msgid "This response provides resource hints (%(hints)s)."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/link.py:144
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `Link` header advertises the following\n"
"[resource hints](https://www.w3.org/TR/resource-hints/), allowing the "
"client to begin work on\n"
"related resources before the current response is fully processed:\n"
"\n"
"%(detail_lines)s\n"
"\n"
"`preload` triggers the browser to fetch a resource needed for the current"
" page; `preconnect`\n"
"opens a connection (DNS + TCP + TLS) to an origin in advance; `dns-"
"prefetch` performs a DNS\n"
"lookup only. Used appropriately, these hints can reduce critical-path "
"latency."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/link.py:159
#, python-format
msgid "The %(rel)s Link target isn't a valid URI."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/link.py:160
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `Link` header advertises a `%(rel)s` resource hint for `%(link)s`, "
"but that isn't a valid URI\n"
"(for example, it may have a malformed IP address in its host). Browsers "
"may ignore this hint."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/link.py:168
#, python-format
msgid "The %(rel)s Link target uses an unsupported scheme."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/link.py:169
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `Link` header advertises a `%(rel)s` resource hint for `%(link)s`, "
"but its scheme\n"
"(`%(scheme)s`) is not `http` or `https`. Browsers will ignore this hint."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/link.py:177
msgid "The 'rev' parameter on the Link header is deprecated."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/link.py:178
msgid ""
"The `Link` header, defined by [RFC 8288](https://www.rfc-"
"editor.org/rfc/rfc8288#section-3), uses the\n"
"`rel` parameter to communicate the type of a link. `rev` is deprecated by"
" that specification\n"
"because it is often confusing.\n"
"\n"
"Use `rel` and an appropriate relation."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/link.py:189
#, python-format
msgid "The 'anchor' parameter on the %(link)s Link header isn't a URI."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/link.py:190
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `Link` header, defined by [RFC 8288](https://www.rfc-"
"editor.org/rfc/rfc8288#section-3), uses the\n"
"`anchor` parameter to define the context URI for the link.\n"
"\n"
"This parameter can be an absolute or relative URI; however, `%(anchor)s` "
"is neither."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/link.py:200
#, python-format
msgid "The 'type' parameter on the %(link)s Link header isn't a media type."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/link.py:201
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `Link` header, defined by [RFC 8288](https://www.rfc-"
"editor.org/rfc/rfc8288#section-3), uses the\n"
"`type` parameter to define the media type of the link target.\n"
"\n"
"However, `%(type)s` is not a valid media type."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/location.py:54
msgid "This status code doesn't define any meaning for the Location header."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/location.py:55
msgid ""
"The `Location` header is used for specific purposes in HTTP; mostly to "
"indicate the URI of another\n"
"resource (e.g., in redirection, or when a new resource is created).\n"
"\n"
"In other status codes (such as this one) it doesn't have a defined "
"meaning, so any use of it won't\n"
"be interoperable.\n"
"\n"
"Sometimes `Location` is confused with `Content-Location`, which indicates"
" a URI for the payload of\n"
"the message that it appears in."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/location.py:69
msgid "The Location header isn't a valid URI."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/location.py:70
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `Location` header's value, `%(uri)s`, can't be resolved as a URI (for"
" example, it may have a\n"
"malformed IP address in its host), so clients won't be able to follow it."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/location.py:78
msgid "The Location header contains a relative URI."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/location.py:79
#, python-format
msgid ""
"`Location` was originally specified to contain an absolute, not relative,"
" URI.\n"
"\n"
"It is in the process of being updated, and most clients will work around "
"this.\n"
"\n"
"The correct absolute URI is (probably): `%(full_uri)s`"
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/max_forwards.py:14
msgid "The Max-Forwards header is ignored for this method."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/max_forwards.py:15
msgid ""
"The `Max-Forwards` header is only defined for `TRACE` and `OPTIONS` "
"requests; for other methods, it\n"
"is likely to be ignored."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/nel.py:182
msgid "The NEL header has an invalid structure."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/nel.py:183
msgid "The `NEL` header should be a list of objects.\n"
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/nel.py:191
#, python-format
msgid "The NEL policy is missing the '%(key)s' key."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/nel.py:192
#, python-format
msgid "The `%(key)s` key is required in `NEL` policies."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/nel.py:199
#, python-format
msgid "The NEL policy has an invalid type for '%(key)s'."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/nel.py:200 httplint/field/parsers/report_to.py:72
#, python-format
msgid "The `%(key)s` key must be of type %(expected)s."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/nel.py:207
#, python-format
msgid "The NEL policy has an invalid value for '%(key)s'."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/nel.py:208
#, python-format
msgid "The `%(key)s` key has an invalid value; %(details)s."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/nel.py:215
msgid "Network Error Logging is configured for this response."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/nel.py:216
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `NEL` header configures\n"
"[Network Error Logging](https://w3c.github.io/network-error-logging/), "
"which instructs the browser\n"
"to report network-level errors (DNS, TCP, TLS, and HTTP failures) to the "
"reporting endpoint(s):\n"
"%(endpoints)s.\n"
"\n"
"This supports observability of failures that would otherwise be invisible"
" to the server."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/nel.py:228
#, python-format
msgid "The reporting endpoint '%(value)s' is not defined."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/nel.py:229
msgid ""
"The `report_to` member in the [Network Error "
"Logging](https://w3c.github.io/network-error-logging/)\n"
"policy specifies a reporting endpoint, but no matching endpoint refers to"
" it in the\n"
"`Reporting-Endpoints` header or a group in the `Report-To` header."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/nel.py:238
#, python-format
msgid "The Report-To group '%(value)s' has no usable endpoint."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/nel.py:239
msgid ""
"The `report_to` member in the [Network Error "
"Logging](https://w3c.github.io/network-error-logging/)\n"
"policy names a group in the `Report-To` header, but none of the group's "
"endpoints has a\n"
"well-formed URL with a secure scheme, so browsers may not deliver reports"
" to it."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/origin.py:71
#, python-format
msgid "%(value)s is not a valid origin."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/origin.py:72
msgid ""
"The Origin header must contain a list of serialized origins (scheme, "
"host, and optional port), or\n"
"the string \"null\"."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/origin.py:80
msgid "The Origin header contains a port with too many digits."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/origin.py:81
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The port in the `Origin` header has more than %(max_digits)s significant "
"digits (leading zeros\n"
"don't count), which is more than recipients can be expected to handle. "
"The whole `Origin` value\n"
"is ignored."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/origin.py:90
msgid "The Origin header contains multiple values."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/origin.py:91
msgid ""
"The `Origin` header should only contain a single value. Any values after "
"the first\n"
"will be ignored."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/permissions_policy.py:89
msgid "This response sets a Permissions Policy."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/permissions_policy.py:90
msgid ""
"The `Permissions-Policy` header allows a site to control the use of "
"browser features."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/permissions_policy.py:97
#, python-format
msgid "The '%(feature)s' feature is allowed for all origins."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/permissions_policy.py:98
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `%(feature)s` feature is allowed for all origins (using `*`).\n"
"This is insecure and should be restricted to specific origins or `self`."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/permissions_policy.py:106
#, python-format
msgid "The value for '%(feature)s' should be an Inner List or the token '*'."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/permissions_policy.py:107
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The value for the `%(feature)s` feature in `Permissions-Policy` is "
"invalid. It should be either\n"
"an Inner List of origins (e.g., `(self \"https://example.com\")`) or the "
"special token `*`."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/permissions_policy.py:115
#, python-format
msgid "'%(token)s' is not valid in an allowlist."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/permissions_policy.py:116
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The token `%(token)s` is not a valid keyword in an allowlist.\n"
"Valid tokens are `self`, `src` and `*`."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/permissions_policy.py:124
#, python-format
msgid "The value '%(value)s' looks like a keyword but is a string."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/permissions_policy.py:125
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The value `%(value)s` is a string, but it looks like a keyword.\n"
"If you meant to use the keyword, remove the quotes (e.g., `self` instead "
"of `\"self\"`)."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/permissions_policy.py:133
#, python-format
msgid "The item '%(item)s' is not a valid type for an allowlist."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/permissions_policy.py:134
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The item `%(item)s` is not a valid type for an allowlist.\n"
"Allowlists should contain origins (strings) or keywords (tokens)."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/pragma.py:37
msgid "The Pragma header is being used in an undefined way."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/pragma.py:38
msgid ""
"HTTP only defines `Pragma: no-cache`; other uses of this header are "
"deprecated."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/proxy_status.py:125
msgid "Information about intermediaries is available."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/proxy_status.py:126
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `Proxy-Status` header field indicates how intermediaries have handled"
" the response.\n"
"\n"
"%(status)s\n"
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/proxy_status.py:136
#, python-format
msgid "A Proxy-Status member is %(member_type)s, not a String or Token."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/proxy_status.py:137
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Each member of the `Proxy-Status` list identifies the intermediary that "
"inserted it, and\n"
"[RFC 9209](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9209.html#section-2) "
"requires it to be a String or\n"
"a Token. This member, `%(value)s`, is %(member_type)s."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/proxy_status.py:146
#, python-format
msgid "The Proxy-Status header has an unknown parameter '%(param)s'."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/proxy_status.py:147
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `%(param)s` parameter is not defined in the Proxy-Status "
"specification.\n"
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/proxy_status.py:155
#, python-format
msgid "The Proxy-Status header has an unknown value for '%(param)s'."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/range.py:127
msgid "The Range header is invalid."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/range.py:128
msgid ""
"The values indicated by the `Range` header are not valid. The first "
"position must be less\n"
"than or equal to the last position."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/range.py:136
msgid "The Range header value isn't valid."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/range.py:137
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The value for this field doesn't conform to its specified syntax; "
"%(problem)s.\n"
"\n"
"See [its definition](%(ref_uri)s) for more information."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/referer.py:71
msgid "The Referer header isn't a valid URI."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/referer.py:72
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `Referer` header's value, `%(uri)s`, can't be parsed as a URI (for "
"example, it may have a\n"
"malformed IP address in its host), so recipients can't make use of it."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/referer.py:80
msgid "The Referer header is sent from a secure origin to an insecure target."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/referer.py:81
msgid ""
"HTTP prohibits a user agent from sending a Referer header field in an "
"unsecured HTTP request\n"
"if the referring resource was accessed with a secure protocol.\n"
"\n"
"See [RFC 9110 Section 10.1.3](https://www.rfc-"
"editor.org/rfc/rfc9110.html#section-10.1.3)\n"
"for details."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/referer.py:92
msgid "The Referer header is sent from a secure origin to a different origin."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/referer.py:93
msgid ""
"HTTP prohibits a user agent from sending a Referer header field if the "
"referring resource was\n"
"accessed with a secure protocol and the request target has an origin "
"differing from that of the\n"
"referring resource, unless the referring resource explicitly allows "
"Referer to be sent.\n"
"\n"
"See [RFC 9110 Section 10.1.3](https://www.rfc-"
"editor.org/rfc/rfc9110.html#section-10.1.3)\n"
"for details."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/referrer_policy.py:46
#, python-format
msgid "This response's Referrer-Policy ('%(policy)s') restricts referrer leakage."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/referrer_policy.py:47
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `Referrer-Policy` value `%(policy)s` prevents the full URL from being"
" sent as a referrer to\n"
"less-secure or cross-origin destinations, reducing the risk of leaking "
"sensitive information in\n"
"the `Referer` request header."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/referrer_policy.py:56
msgid "This response's Referrer-Policy allows unsafe URLs."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/referrer_policy.py:57
msgid ""
"Using `unsafe-url` in `Referrer-Policy` means that the full URL "
"(including query parameters) will\n"
"be sent as a referrer to all origins, including those that are not secure"
" (HTTP). This can leak\n"
"sensitive information."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/referrer_policy.py:66
#, python-format
msgid "The Referrer-Policy value '%(policy)s' is unknown."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/referrer_policy.py:67
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `Referrer-Policy` header contains the value `%(policy)s`, which is "
"not a known referrer policy.\n"
"It will be ignored by browsers."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/referrer_policy.py:75
msgid "No valid Referrer-Policy found."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/referrer_policy.py:76
msgid ""
"The `Referrer-Policy` header does not contain any valid policies. "
"Browsers will use their default\n"
"policy (usually `strict-origin-when-cross-origin`)."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/referrer_policy.py:84
#, python-format
msgid "Multiple Referrer-Policy values found; only '%(effective)s' is used."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/referrer_policy.py:85
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `Referrer-Policy` header contains multiple valid policies. Browsers "
"will only use the last\n"
"valid policy found, which is `%(effective)s`. Earlier values are ignored."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/report_to.py:54
msgid "The Report-To header value has an invalid structure."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/report_to.py:55
msgid "The `Report-To` header should be a list of objects.\n"
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/report_to.py:63
#, python-format
msgid "The Report-To header value is missing the '%(key)s' key."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/report_to.py:64
#, python-format
msgid "The `%(key)s` key is required in `Report-To` objects."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/report_to.py:71
#, python-format
msgid "The Report-To header has an invalid type for '%(key)s'."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/reporting_endpoints.py:56
#, python-format
msgid "The %(name)s reporting endpoint is not secure."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/reporting_endpoints.py:57
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The reporting endpoint `%(name)s` uses an insecure URL (`%(url)s`). "
"Browsers may ignore it."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/reporting_endpoints.py:64
#, python-format
msgid "The %(name)s reporting endpoint isn't a valid URL."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/reporting_endpoints.py:65
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The reporting endpoint `%(name)s` has a URL (`%(url)s`) that can't be "
"resolved (for example, it may\n"
"have a malformed IP address in its host). Browsers may ignore it."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/reporting_endpoints.py:73
#, python-format
msgid "The %(name)s reporting endpoint is invalid."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/reporting_endpoints.py:74
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The reporting endpoint `%(name)s` must be a string URL.\n"
"Found: `%(value)s` (type `%(found_type)s`)."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/server.py:64
msgid "The Server header is long."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/server.py:65
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `Server` header is %(server_length)s long, which uses unnecessary "
"bandwidth\n"
"and can expose details of the back-end system to attackers.\n"
"\n"
"Consider shortening it."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/server_timing.py:61
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The '%(param)s' parameter on the '%(metric)s' metric has a non-numeric "
"value."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/server_timing.py:62
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `%(param)s` parameter on the `%(metric)s` metric of the Server-Timing"
" header requires a\n"
"valid number, but `%(value)s` was found.\n"
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/server_timing.py:71
#, python-format
msgid "The '%(metric)s' metric is missing the 'dur' parameter."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/server_timing.py:72
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `%(metric)s` metric in the Server-Timing header is missing the `dur` "
"(duration) parameter.\n"
"\n"
"This parameter isn't required, but without it browsers may not be able to"
" usefully display it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/server_timing.py:82
#, python-format
msgid "The '%(metric)s' metric is missing the 'desc' parameter."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/server_timing.py:83
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `%(metric)s` metric in the Server-Timing header is missing the `desc`"
" (description) parameter.\n"
"\n"
"Descriptions can help contextualise a metric when displayed.\n"
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/set_cookie.py:436
msgid "The response URI could not be parsed, so a default Path of / was used."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/set_cookie.py:437
msgid ""
"The URI that this response was retrieved from, as given to the linter, is"
" not valid, so it can't\n"
"be used. A `Path` attribute in `Set-Cookie` that is empty, or doesn't "
"start with `/`, is replaced\n"
"by the default path of the request URI; because that URI is unusable, `/`"
" was used instead."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/set_cookie.py:446
msgid "This response has a Set-Cookie header without a cookie-name."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/set_cookie.py:447
msgid ""
"This `Set-Cookie` header has an empty name; there needs to be a name "
"before the `=`.\n"
"\n"
"Browsers will ignore this cookie."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/set_cookie.py:456
#, python-format
msgid "The %(cookie_name)s cookie has an invalid Expires date."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/set_cookie.py:457
msgid ""
"The `expires` date on this `Set-Cookie` header isn't valid; see\n"
"[RFC6265](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6265) for details of the "
"correct format."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/set_cookie.py:465
#, python-format
msgid "The %(cookie_name)s cookie has an empty Max-Age."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/set_cookie.py:466
msgid ""
"The `max-age` parameter on this `Set-Cookie` header doesn't have a value."
"\n"
"\n"
"Browsers will ignore the `max-age` value as a result."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/set_cookie.py:475
#, python-format
msgid "The %(cookie_name)s cookie has a Max-Age with a leading zero."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/set_cookie.py:476
msgid ""
"The `max-age` parameter on this `Set-Cookie` header has a leading zero, "
"which the `Set-Cookie`\n"
"grammar doesn't allow.\n"
"\n"
"Browsers may still read it as an ordinary number."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/set_cookie.py:486
#, python-format
msgid "The %(cookie_name)s cookie has a negative Max-Age."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/set_cookie.py:487
msgid ""
"The `max-age` parameter on this `Set-Cookie` header is negative.\n"
"\n"
"The grammar that servers are to follow\n"
"([RFC6265 section 4.1.1](https://www.rfc-"
"editor.org/rfc/rfc6265.html#section-4.1.1)) only allows\n"
"a `max-age` that starts with a non-zero digit. However, browsers may "
"accept a leading `-`\n"
"([section 5.2.2](https://www.rfc-"
"editor.org/rfc/rfc6265.html#section-5.2.2)), and expire the\n"
"cookie immediately."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/set_cookie.py:500
#, python-format
msgid "The %(cookie_name)s cookie has a non-numeric Max-Age."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/set_cookie.py:501
msgid ""
"The `max-age` parameter on this `Set-Cookie` header isn't numeric.\n"
"\n"
"Browsers will ignore the `max-age` value as a result."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/set_cookie.py:510
#, python-format
msgid "The %(cookie_name)s cookie has an empty domain."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/set_cookie.py:511
msgid ""
"The `domain` parameter on this `Set-Cookie` header is empty.\n"
"\n"
"Note that handling of empty domains is \n"
"[not interoperable](https://chromestatus.com/feature/5674723800252416).\n"
"\n"
"Browsers will probably ignore it as a result."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/set_cookie.py:523
#, python-format
msgid "The %(cookie_name)s cookie is missing the Secure attribute."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/set_cookie.py:524
msgid ""
"The `Secure` attribute on this `Set-Cookie` header is missing.\n"
"\n"
"Because the `SameSite` attribute is set to `None`, the `Secure` attribute"
" is required.\n"
"\n"
"Browsers will ignore this cookie."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/set_cookie.py:535
#, python-format
msgid "The %(cookie_name)s cookie has an unknown attribute, '%(attribute)s'."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/set_cookie.py:536
#, python-format
msgid ""
"This cookie has an extra parameter, `%(attribute)s`.\n"
"\n"
"Browsers will ignore it."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/set_cookie.py:545
msgid "The 'Priority' Set-Cookie attribute is deprecated."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/set_cookie.py:546
msgid "The `Priority` attribute was an experiment, and is no longer supported.\n"
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/set_cookie.py:554
msgid "The 'Version Set-Cookie attribute is deprecated."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/set_cookie.py:555
msgid ""
"The `Version` attribute is no longer part of the `Set-Cookie` "
"specification,\n"
"and is ignored by browsers.\n"
"\n"
"Because some software still interprets cookies differently when it is "
"present,\n"
"[it can cause security \n"
"issues](https://portswigger.net/research/bypassing-wafs-with-the-phantom-"
"version-cookie).\n"
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/set_cookie.py:568
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The %(cookie_name)s cookie has an unknown '%(attribute_name)s' attribute "
"value."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/set_cookie.py:569
#, python-format
msgid ""
"This `Set-Cookie` header has an unknown `%(attribute_name)s` attribute "
"value, `%(attribute_value)s`.\n"
"\n"
"Browsers will probably ignore it as a result."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/set_cookie.py:578
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The %(cookie_name)s cookie has the Partitioned attribute but is missing "
"the Secure attribute."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/set_cookie.py:582
msgid ""
"The `Partitioned` attribute on this `Set-Cookie` header is present, but "
"the `Secure` attribute is\n"
"missing.\n"
"\n"
"Browsers will ignore the `Partitioned` attribute as a result."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/set_cookie.py:592
#, python-format
msgid "The %(cookie_name)s Set-Cookie header is too large."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/set_cookie.py:593
msgid ""
"The `Set-Cookie` header is larger than 4096 bytes.\n"
"\n"
"Browsers will ignore this cookie."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/set_cookie.py:602
#, python-format
msgid "The %(cookie_name)s Set-Cookie value is large."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/set_cookie.py:603
#, python-format
msgid "This `Set-Cookie` value is %(set_cookie_value_length)s long.\n"
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/set_cookie.py:618
#, python-format
msgid "The %(cookie_name)s Set-Cookie header has a lifetime that is too long."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/set_cookie.py:619
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `Set-Cookie` header has a lifetime (Max-Age or Expires) of "
"%(duration)s, which is greater than\n"
"400 days.\n"
"\n"
"Browsers will cap the lifetime to 400 days."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/set_cookie.py:629
#, python-format
msgid "The %(cookie_name)s Set-Cookie header requires the Secure attribute."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/set_cookie.py:630
msgid ""
"The `Set-Cookie` header has a prefix (e.g., `__Secure-` or `__Host-`) "
"that requires the `Secure`\n"
"attribute.\n"
"\n"
"Browsers will reject this cookie."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/set_cookie.py:640
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The %(cookie_name)s Set-Cookie header has a __Host- prefix but sets a "
"Domain."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/set_cookie.py:641
msgid ""
"The `Set-Cookie` header has a `__Host-` prefix, but it sets a `Domain` "
"attribute.\n"
"\n"
"Browsers will reject this cookie."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/set_cookie.py:650
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The %(cookie_name)s Set-Cookie header has a __Host- prefix but does not "
"set Path=/."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/set_cookie.py:651
msgid ""
"The `Set-Cookie` header has a `__Host-` prefix, but it does not set "
"`Path=/`.\n"
"\n"
"Browsers will reject this cookie."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/set_cookie.py:660
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The %(cookie_name)s Set-Cookie header has duplicate '%(attribute)s' "
"attributes."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/set_cookie.py:661
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `%(attribute)s` attribute appears more than once in this `Set-Cookie`"
" header.\n"
"\n"
"Browsers will only use the last occurrence."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/set_cookie.py:670
msgid "This response sets cookies restricted with Secure, HttpOnly, and SameSite."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/set_cookie.py:671
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The following cookies set `Secure` (only sent over HTTPS), `HttpOnly` "
"(inaccessible to\n"
"JavaScript), and a non-`None` `SameSite` value (limiting cross-site "
"sending):\n"
"\n"
"%(cookie_names)s.\n"
"\n"
"Together, these attributes substantially reduce a cookie's exposure to "
"common attacks such as\n"
"theft over plaintext connections, cross-site scripting, and cross-site "
"request forgery."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/set_cookie.py:684
msgid "This response sets duplicate cookies."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/set_cookie.py:685
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The following cookies are set more than once in this response: "
"`%(cookie_names)s`.\n"
"\n"
"Browsers will likely accept all of them, but the order of application\n"
"may vary or be confusing."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/speculation_rules.py:48
msgid "The speculation rule URL is not secure."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/speculation_rules.py:49
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The speculation rule `%(url)s` uses an insecure URL. Browsers may ignore "
"it."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/speculation_rules.py:56
msgid "The speculation rule URL isn't valid."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/speculation_rules.py:57
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The speculation rule `%(url)s` can't be resolved as a URL (for example, "
"it may have a malformed IP\n"
"address in its host). Browsers may ignore it."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/speculation_rules.py:65
msgid "The speculation rule value is invalid."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/speculation_rules.py:66
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The speculation rule is a\n"
"[Structured Field](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8941.html) list of "
"Items, where\n"
"each item must be a string URL. Found: `%(value)s` (type "
"`%(found_type)s`)."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/strict_transport_security.py:212
msgid "Strict Transport Security (HSTS) is enabled."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/strict_transport_security.py:213
msgid ""
"This site has enabled HTTP Strict Transport Security (HSTS), which tells "
"the browser to only\n"
"communicate with it over a secure connection."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/strict_transport_security.py:221
msgid "This response's Strict Transport Security (HSTS) header is invalid."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/strict_transport_security.py:222
msgid ""
"This site has attempted to enable HTTP Strict Transport Security (HSTS), "
"which tells the browser to only\n"
"communicate with it over a secure connection.\n"
"\n"
"However, one or more issues prevent it from being valid. See the child "
"notes for details."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/strict_transport_security.py:232
msgid "There is no max-age directive."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/strict_transport_security.py:233
msgid ""
"The `Strict-Transport-Security` header requires a `max-age` directive to "
"be valid."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/strict_transport_security.py:240
msgid "The max-age is 0."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/strict_transport_security.py:241
msgid ""
"A `max-age` of 0 tells the browser to expire the `Strict-Transport-"
"Security` policy immediately,\n"
"effectively disabling it."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/strict_transport_security.py:249
msgid "The max-age is less than one year."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/strict_transport_security.py:250
msgid ""
"Most sites should set a `max-age` of at least one year on `Strict-"
"Transport-Security`."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/strict_transport_security.py:257
msgid "HSTS applies to subdomains."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/strict_transport_security.py:258
msgid ""
"The `includeSubDomains` directive indicates that this HSTS policy applies"
" to this domain as well as\n"
"all of its subdomains."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/strict_transport_security.py:266
msgid "HSTS doesn't apply to subdomains."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/strict_transport_security.py:267
msgid ""
"The `includeSubDomains` directive indicates that this HSTS policy applies"
" to this domain as well as\n"
"all of its subdomains.\n"
"\n"
"Because cookies can be set across HTTP and HTTPS sites as well as across "
"subdomains, this means \n"
"that an attacker might be able to take advantage of a subdomain that "
"doesn't have HSTS enabled.\n"
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/strict_transport_security.py:279
msgid "Browser preloading is allowed."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/strict_transport_security.py:280
msgid ""
"The `preload` directive on `Strict-Transport-Security` allows browsers to"
" preload the site in\n"
"its HSTS lists, avoiding the potential for making unencrypted requests "
"when first accessing the\n"
"site.\n"
"\n"
"See the [HSTS Preload List](https://hstspreload.org/) for more "
"information.\n"
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/strict_transport_security.py:292
msgid "Browser preloading is allowed, but this policy isn't suitable for it."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/strict_transport_security.py:293
msgid ""
"Preloading a site in a browser's HSTS list requires a `max-age` of at "
"least one year and the\n"
"`includeSubDomains` directive.\n"
"\n"
"See the [HSTS Preload List](https://hstspreload.org/) for more "
"information.\n"
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/strict_transport_security.py:304
msgid "Browser preloading isn't allowed."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/strict_transport_security.py:305
msgid ""
"Without a `preload` directive, browsers may make an unencrypted request "
"when first accessing the\n"
"site, potentially exposing sensitive information.\n"
"\n"
"See the [HSTS Preload List](https://hstspreload.org/) for more "
"information.\n"
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/strict_transport_security.py:316
msgid "The HSTS header contains a duplicate directive."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/strict_transport_security.py:317
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `%(directive)s` directive appears more than once in the `Strict-"
"Transport-Security` header.\n"
"Directives must only appear once."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/strict_transport_security.py:325
msgid "The Strict-Transport-Security header has a trailing semicolon."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/strict_transport_security.py:326
msgid ""
"The `Strict-Transport-Security` header ends with a semicolon. The grammar"
" allows this, but some\n"
"implementations may be confused by it."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/strict_transport_security.py:334
msgid "The HSTS header is sent over HTTP."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/strict_transport_security.py:335
msgid ""
"The `Strict-Transport-Security` header is ignored when sent over HTTP, "
"regardless of the status\n"
"code (including a redirect to HTTPS). It should only be sent over HTTPS."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/strict_transport_security.py:343
msgid "The max-age directive in the HSTS header is invalid."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/strict_transport_security.py:344
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `max-age` directive in the `Strict-Transport-Security` header must be"
" a non-negative\n"
"integer. Its value is not valid:\n"
"\n"
"%(max_age)s"
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/strict_transport_security.py:354
#, python-format
msgid "The %(directive)s directive in the HSTS header must not have a value."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/strict_transport_security.py:355
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `%(directive)s` directive in the `Strict-Transport-Security` header "
"is a valueless\n"
"directive. It should not have an associated value."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/sunset.py:24
msgid "The resource has Sunset."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/sunset.py:25
msgid ""
"The `Sunset` header indicates that this resource has already passed its "
"sunset date and may become\n"
"unresponsive."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/transfer_encoding.py:73
msgid "The identity transfer-coding isn't necessary."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/transfer_encoding.py:74
msgid ""
"HTTP defines _transfer-codings_ as a hop-by-hop encoding of the message's"
" content. The `identity`\n"
"transfer-coding was defined as the absence of encoding; it doesn't do "
"anything, so it is unnecessary.\n"
"\n"
"You can remove this token to save a few bytes."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/transfer_encoding.py:84
#, python-format
msgid ""
"This response uses the '%(coding)s' transfer-coding, but it wasn't "
"requested."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/transfer_encoding.py:85
#, python-format
msgid ""
"This response's `Transfer-Encoding` header indicates it has the "
"`%(coding)s` transfer-coding applied,\n"
"but the client didn't indicate support for it in the request.\n"
"\n"
"Normally, clients ask for the encodings they want in the `TE` request "
"header. Using codings that\n"
"the client doesn't explicitly request can lead to interoperability "
"problems."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/transfer_encoding.py:96
msgid "This message had parameters on its transfer-codings."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/transfer_encoding.py:97
msgid ""
"HTTP allows transfer-codings in the `Transfer-Encoding` header to have "
"optional parameters, but it\n"
"doesn't define what they mean.\n"
"\n"
"This message has encodings with such parameters; although they're "
"technically allowed, they may\n"
"cause interoperability problems. They should be removed."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/use_as_dictionary.py:78
#, python-format
msgid "The %(field_name)s parameter '%(param)s' has an invalid type."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/use_as_dictionary.py:79
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The `%(field_name)s` parameter `%(param)s` must be a `%(expected)s`. "
"Found `%(got)s`."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/use_as_dictionary.py:86
msgid "The match-dest parameter has an invalid type."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/use_as_dictionary.py:87
msgid "The `match-dest` parameter must be an Inner List of Strings."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/use_as_dictionary.py:94
msgid "The Use-As-Dictionary header does not have a match parameter."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/use_as_dictionary.py:95
msgid ""
"The `match` parameter MUST be included for the dictionary to be "
"considered valid, so this\n"
"dictionary will not be used."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/vary.py:45
msgid "Vary: * effectively makes this response uncacheable."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/vary.py:46
msgid ""
"`Vary *` indicates that responses for this resource vary by some aspect "
"that can't (or won't) be\n"
"described by the server. This makes this response effectively uncacheable."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/vary.py:54
msgid "Vary: User-Agent can cause cache inefficiency."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/vary.py:55
msgid ""
"Sending `Vary: User-Agent` requires caches to store a separate copy of "
"the response for every\n"
"`User-Agent` request header they see.\n"
"\n"
"Since there are so many different `User-Agent`s, this can \"bloat\" "
"caches with many copies of the\n"
"same thing, or cause them to give up on storing these responses at all.\n"
"\n"
"Consider having different URIs for the various versions of your content "
"instead; this will give\n"
"finer control over caching without sacrificing efficiency."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/vary.py:69
msgid "Vary: Host is not necessary."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/vary.py:70
msgid ""
"Some servers (e.g., [Apache](http://httpd.apache.org/) with\n"
"[mod_rewrite](http://httpd.apache.org/docs/2.4/mod/mod_rewrite.html)) "
"will send `Host` in the\n"
"`Vary` header, in the belief that this is necessary.\n"
"\n"
"This is not the case; HTTP specifies that the URI is the basis of the "
"cache key, and the URI\n"
"incorporates the `Host` header.\n"
"\n"
"The presence of `Vary: Host` may make some caches not store an otherwise "
"cacheable response (since\n"
"some cache implementations will not store anything that has a `Vary` "
"header)."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/vary.py:85
msgid "Transparent Content Negotiation is not widely supported."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/vary.py:86
msgid ""
"The `Vary: Negotiate` header value is not necessary, as \n"
"[Transparent Content Negotiation](https://www.rfc-"
"editor.org/rfc/rfc2295.html)\n"
"is not widely supported.\n"
"\n"
"Consider removing it."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/vary.py:97
msgid "The Vary header contains duplicate values."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/vary.py:98
msgid ""
"The `Vary` header allows you to list the parts of the request that "
"effectively change the response\n"
"representation.\n"
"\n"
"Listing the same header more than once is redundant and can be confusing."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/vary.py:108
#, python-format
msgid "This resource varies in %(vary_count)s ways."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/vary.py:109
msgid ""
"The `Vary` mechanism allows a resource to describe the dimensions that "
"its responses vary, or\n"
"change, over; each listed header is another dimension.\n"
"\n"
"Varying by too many dimensions makes using this information impractical."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/via.py:37
msgid "One or more intermediaries are present."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/via.py:38
msgid ""
"The `Via` header indicates that one or more intermediaries are present "
"between the user agent and\n"
"the origin server for the resource.\n"
"\n"
"This may indicate that a proxy is configured, or that the server uses a "
"\"reverse proxy\" or CDN in\n"
"front of it.\n"
"\n"
"There field has three space-separated components; first, the HTTP version"
" of the message that the\n"
"intermediary received, then the identity of the intermediary (usually but"
" not always its hostname),\n"
"and then optionally a product identifier or comment (usually used to "
"identify the software being\n"
"used)."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/x_content_type_options.py:27
msgid "This response instructs browsers not to 'sniff' its media type."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/x_content_type_options.py:30
msgid ""
"Many Web browsers \"sniff\" the media type of responses to figure out "
"whether they're HTML, RSS or\n"
"another format, no matter what the `Content-Type` header says.\n"
"\n"
"This header instructs browsers not to do this, but to always respect the\n"
"Content-Type header. It probably won't have any effect in other clients.\n"
"\n"
"See [MDN](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/X"
"-Content-Type-Options)\n"
"for more information about this header."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/x_content_type_options.py:44
msgid "X-Content-Type-Options contains an unknown value."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/x_content_type_options.py:47
msgid ""
"Only one value is currently defined for this header, `nosniff`. Using "
"other values here won't\n"
"necessarily cause problems, but they probably won't have any effect "
"either.\n"
"\n"
"See [MDN](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/X"
"-Content-Type-Options)\n"
"for more information about this header."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/x_frame_options.py:56
msgid "This response prevents browsers from rendering it within a frame."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/x_frame_options.py:57
msgid ""
"The `DENY` value of `X-Frame-Options` prevents this content from being "
"rendered within a frame,\n"
"defending against clickjacking-style attacks.\n"
"\n"
"Note that `X-Frame-Options` has been superseded by the\n"
"[`frame-ancestors`](https://www.w3.org/TR/CSP3/#directive-frame-"
"ancestors) directive of\n"
"`Content-Security-Policy`, which offers finer-grained control and is the "
"modern equivalent.\n"
"If both are present, browsers that support CSP will use `frame-ancestors`"
" and ignore this header.\n"
"\n"
"See [MDN](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/X"
"-Frame-Options) for more information.\n"
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/x_frame_options.py:73
msgid ""
"This response prevents browsers from rendering it within a frame on "
"another site."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/x_frame_options.py:74
msgid ""
"The `SAMEORIGIN` value of `X-Frame-Options` prevents this content from "
"being rendered within a\n"
"frame on a different origin, defending against clickjacking-style "
"attacks.\n"
"\n"
"Note that `X-Frame-Options` has been superseded by the\n"
"[`frame-ancestors`](https://www.w3.org/TR/CSP3/#directive-frame-"
"ancestors) directive of\n"
"`Content-Security-Policy`, which offers finer-grained control and is the "
"modern equivalent.\n"
"If both are present, browsers that support CSP will use `frame-ancestors`"
" and ignore this header.\n"
"\n"
"See [MDN](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/X"
"-Frame-Options) for more information.\n"
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/x_frame_options.py:90
msgid "The X-Frame-Options header uses the obsolete ALLOW-FROM value."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/x_frame_options.py:91
msgid ""
"[RFC 7034](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7034) defined an `ALLOW-"
"FROM` value for this header, but\n"
"it is obsolete, and browsers may ignore it. Use the\n"
"[`frame-ancestors`](https://www.w3.org/TR/CSP3/#directive-frame-"
"ancestors) directive of\n"
"`Content-Security-Policy` to allow framing by specific origins.\n"
"\n"
"See [MDN](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/X"
"-Frame-Options) for more information.\n"
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/x_frame_options.py:104
msgid "The X-Frame-Options header contains an unknown value."
msgstr ""

#: httplint/field/parsers/x_frame_options.py:107
msgid ""
"Browsers act on only two values for this header, `DENY` and `SAMEORIGIN`."
" Using other values here\n"
"won't necessarily cause problems, but they probably won't have any effect"
" either.\n"
"\n"
"See [MDN](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/X"
"-Frame-Options) for more information.\n"
msgstr ""

